This parameter was intented for a former version of Appendix G, but the requirement is stil in CCS TSI 6.1.1.2. """@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/etcsTransmitsTrackConditions
:etcsTransmitsTrackConditions rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf :tsiCompliantTrainProtectionSystemDataParameter ;
                              rdfs:domain :ETCS ;
                              rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
                              :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
                              :dependencyNote "A value has to be provided when ETCS is present (a value is provided on 1.1.1.3.2.1)."@en ;
                              :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                              :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.2.12" ,
                                         "1.2.1.1.1.12" ;
                              :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/EtcsTransmitsTrackConditions> ,
                                                        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/EtcsTransmitsTrackConditionsApplicability> ;
                              :tsiOPEAppendixD3Index "1.1" ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                  "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                  "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :etcsLevelType ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
                              rdfs:comment """If the trackside does not provide Track Conditions, the driver will need to be informed about such conditions via alternative methods.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en ;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                              rdfs:label "Is the ETCS trackside engineered to transmit Track Conditions"@en ;
                              rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/domains/technical-specifications-interoperability/control-command-and-signalling-tsi_en#oe-content-paragraph-1632"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]
If the trackside does not provide Track Conditions, the driver will need to be informed about such conditions via alternative methods.
In ETCS level NTC and level 0 track conditions are not managed (at least in Baseline 2)
See: TSI CCS (Subset-026, Chapter 5, section 5.18)"""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/existenceOfIndustrialRisk
:existenceOfIndustrialRisk rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf :routeBookDataParameter ;
                           rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                       :SectionOfLine
                                                     )
                                       ] ;
                           rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
                           :applicable "Y/N" ;
                           :formatNote "Y/N" ;
                           :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                           :rinfIndex "1.1.0.0.1.1" ;
                           :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.2.5" ;
                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2025-01-30"^^xsd:date ;
                           rdfs:comment "Indication that the full section of line (or a part of it) it is identified by the Infrastructure Managers (and communicated to the RU) where drivers are not supposed to get off the locomotive."@en ;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                           rdfs:label "Industrial risks â€” locations where it is dangerous for the driver to step out"@en ;
                           <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Although it is just an indication of existence of an industrial risk, the area covering the industrial risk should be references on the topological network.
For the route book purpose, the industrial risks should be defined as linear references instead of area. SpecialArea of type \"industrial risk\" should be used"""@en .


